This adapter replaces the real library instead of re-exporting it:
classify.py classifies the library as a full-shim even though it exists on
iOS, plans every import so the adapter or a generated stub defines it, and
build_shims.py emits no LC_REEXPORT_DYLIB to the real library, in builds for
one application and in generic builds. The real framework still loads beside
the shim (the AppKit adapter links it for GCMouse raw input), so the guest's
notification constants must not share names with it; see GameController.m.
In a generic build, an import this adapter does not define still resolves to
the real framework through the process-wide fallback.
